#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD0029 expect=skipped domain=LB
#note "dataset LB without the LBSTRESC column; LBSTRESU and LBORRESU are present, LBORRESU populated and LBSTRESU empty on both rows. Requirements.Variables.All [--STRESU, --STRESC, --ORRESU] gates the rule out -> auditable skip naming the absent variable. Discriminating for the All gate's --STRESC member only (not for the verdict): without it the absent LBSTRESC reads as a constant missing value, 'not empty(--STRESC)' is false on every record and the rule would answer noViolation instead of skipped."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col LBORRESU type=Char label="Original Units"
col LBSTRESU type=Char label="Standard Units"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | GLUC | mg/dL |
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 2 | ALB  | g/dL  |
---
